{"message": "For a $10 IPO bid you’ll hit the floor – most US IPOs need at least 100 shares, so you’ll be left with cash. In India the minimum application size is usually ₹15,000, so your ₹10,000 budget can only buy on the secondary market. If you buy Reliance on Zerodha delivery, the round‑trip cost is about ₹38 (0.38%) plus a 20% short‑term capital‑gain tax if you sell within a year – that’s a 20.38% hit on the gross return.

If you’re looking for auto or battery makers, consider Tata Motors (TATAMOTORS.NS), Mahindra & Mahindra (M&M.NS) and Maruti Suzuki (MARUTI.NS) for cars, and Tata Power (TATAPOWER.NS) or Ather Energy (ATHERENERG.NS) for batteries. These are all listed, but their short‑term swings are large and the 10× goal will still require many years or a big out‑of‑the‑box pick.

Mood: neutral", "mood": "neutral", "watch": ["NVDA", "TATAMOTORS.NS", "ATHERENERG.NS"]}
